{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"strategy pattern strategy pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","fileName":"Strategy Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Strategy Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"strategy pattern strategy pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","fileName":"Strategy Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Strategy Pattern","heading":"Strategy Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The strategy pattern defines interchangeable algorithms behind one operation and chooses which one to apply at runtime. A caller can request an outcome without embedding a branch for every algorithm. The book also shows a functional version: a filtering operation accepts a `Func<T, bool>` criterion, so supplying a different predicate changes the selection strategy without adding another class.\n\nStrategy turns a family of algorithms into interchangeable implementations of one abstraction. An object can receive the appropriate behavior through composition, avoiding an inheritance hierarchy that mixes independent behavioral dimensions.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"strategy pattern strategy pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Strategy Pattern.md","fileName":"Strategy Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Strategy Pattern","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}